  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Eribulin is an anticancer medicine used to treat breast cancer and a type of soft-tissue sarcoma called liposarcoma. It is authorised in the European Union and used as an antineoplastic agent for these cancers.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q408717&quot;>Wikidata Q408717</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>eribulin</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>L01XX41</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB08871&quot;>DB08871</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/73425383&quot;>73425383</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:63587&quot;>63587</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q408717&quot;>Q408717</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C40H59NO11</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>729.908 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
